    <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
          <h2 id="faqTitle">Straight answers.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary>What happens in a process review?</summary>
            <p>A free 30-minute call. You tell us where your team&rsquo;s time goes; we tell you honestly whether AI is the answer, which process we&rsquo;d look at first, and what discovery would involve. If AI isn&rsquo;t the right fix, we&rsquo;ll say so.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary>Why pay for discovery?</summary>
            <p>Because it&rsquo;s real work: we map the process, measure the baseline and score every opportunity, and you keep the map whether or not you build with us. It&rsquo;s R7,500, and it comes off your implementation in full if you go ahead within 60 days.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary>Our data is messy. Is that a problem?</summary>
            <p>It&rsquo;s normal. Data availability is one of the six things we score. If it&rsquo;s not ready, we tell you what to fix first rather than building something that can&rsquo;t work.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary>What does Operations actually cover?</summary>
            <p>Monitoring, the model and API costs up to your plan&rsquo;s allowance, maintenance and security updates, usage monitoring, regular evaluation of the system&rsquo;s accuracy, support to a defined response time, hours for workflow improvements and small integrations, and a monthly report that leads with what improved and by how much.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary>What about our data and privacy?</summary>
            <p>Your data stays in accounts you own, is used only to run your system, and is handled under POPIA. Where a wrong answer could cost you, the system drafts and a person approves.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ FINAL CTA ============ -->
    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="ctaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <span class="cta__services">Discovery · Implementation · Operations · Measured ROI</span>
        <h2 id="ctaTitle">Find the work your employees shouldn&rsquo;t be doing.</h2>
        <p>Thirty minutes, free. Bring one process that takes too long.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--light btn--large" data-review-open>Book a process review</button>
          <a href="method" class="btn btn--ghost-light btn--large">See the method</a>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" data-contact-block hidden>Prefer to talk first? <a class="inline-link" href="#" data-contact="whatsapp" hidden>WhatsApp us</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

